  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Accenture Federal Services obligated $257M in FY2027 to date on 57 awards, with an average award size of $4.5M. Obligations fell 92.9% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations before FY2027 ranged from $3B to $3.7B, with FY22 at $3B, FY23 at $3.2B, FY24 at $3.7B, FY25 at $3.5B, and FY26 at $3.6B. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share of FY2027 obligations at $151M, followed by the General Services Administration at $28M and the Department of Energy at $20.3M. Computer Systems Design Services was the dominant market with $247M in obligations, and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounted for $10.5M. These figures are contract obligations unless otherwise noted. Current-year totals are partial because FY2027 is fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest agency customers for FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer at $151M. The General Services Administration follows at $28M and the Department of Energy at $20.3M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $14.6M and the Department of Commerce at $12.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date performance compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 92.9% year over year to $257M in FY2027 to date. Prior fiscal years showed substantially higher totals: FY22 $3B, FY23 $3.2B, FY24 $3.7B, FY25 $3.5B, and FY26 $3.6B."
      }
    ]
  },
